  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordination MD ATP phase 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on long term agreements between Vietnam and the Netherlands in the field of water and agriculture, a joint Netherlands-Vietnamese approach focuses on a multi-year collaboration for the Mekong Delta Agro Transformation, using an innovative governance model for Vietnam that gives direction to the agricultural transformation process. It will be based on the Dutch Delta Programme Model with a multi-stakeholder approach in the form of various substantive working groups. On the one hand, these working groups must provide policy direction and ensure that the right knowledge questions are answered. On the other hand, they must develop business models and ensure that investments take place.In the framework of the Mekong Delta Agro Transformation Plan the project will enhance the cooperation between Vietnam and the Netherlands in the field of water and agriculture development with an open view on energy and logistics in which local sustainable economic development is key. The enhancement of a cohesive and efficient network will facilitate a bilateral relationship focused on knowledge exchange and advisory, ultimately benefiting the Vietnamese private sector and promoting a trade-oriented connection between the two nations.</narrative>
  </description>
